It is Thursday evening, half past five.
I am at the badminton club.
At the reception I rent a racket.
That costs three euros.
Timo, Lena and Max are already waiting on the court.
"Hello everyone!" I call out.
"Did you train well last week?" I ask.
"Yes, we practised a lot," Timo answers.
We play a doubles match.
Timo and I play against Lena and Max.
The game is very fast and is a lot of fun.
"You played wonderfully!" Lena calls out after a rally.
"We scored the point!" I say to Timo.
After an hour we take a break.
Max packs his bag.
"I am saying goodbye," he says.
"I start early tomorrow," he explains.
"Bye, Max!" we say together.
Timo, Lena and I stay a little longer.
